---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const resumeHref = '/Marco_Bacis_CV_Product.pdf';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About Marco Bacis"
	description="Marco Bacis is a senior full-stack engineer working across modern .NET, Angular, and the systems behind application software."
>
	<article class="about-page">
		<header class="about-intro">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
				<h1>I make <br/> software easier <br/> to evolve</h1>
			</div>
			<div class="intro-copy">
				<p class="lead">
					I’m Marco, a senior full-stack engineer with more than seven years of professional experience, 
					currently working at <a href="https://zupit.it">Zupit</a> as a software engineer.
				</p>
				<p>
					My work is strongest in the .NET ecosystem: backend development with C# and modern .NET, 
					frontend applications with Angular and TypeScript, SQL databases, and cloud-hosted business software.
					I also contribute to the work around the code—reviews, technical discussions, release coordination,
					mentoring, and decisions that keep a system maintainable as it changes.
				</p>
			</div>
		</header>

		<div class="about-grid">
			<aside class="about-aside" aria-label="A few facts">
				<p class="aside-label">At a glance</p>
				<dl>
					<div>
						<dt>Based in</dt>
						<dd>Italy</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Current focus</dt>
						<dd>.NET · Angular · Azure · SQL</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Learning next</dt>
						<dd>Architecture · Rust · systems</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
				<a class="aside-link" data-umami-event="click-resume" data-umami-event-placement="about-aside" href={resumeHref}>Read my résumé <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
			</aside>

			<div class="about-content">
				<section aria-labelledby="approach-title">
					<p class="section-label">01 · How I work</p>
					<h2 id="approach-title">&quot;Make the change easy, then make the easy change&quot;</h2>
					<p>
						I care about readable code, tests I can trust, and keeping the system maintainable over time.
						In my day-to-day work, this means thinking about boundaries, persistence, deployment and failure modes
						in addition to the feature itself.
					</p>
					<p>
						I prefer a pragmatic approach over following the current hype.
						Sometimes the right move is to simplify an application: introducing seams,
						improving pipelines, make old code safer to change. 
						Code reviews and technical conversations are part of that work, as are the less visible parts:
						coordinating releases, working with product owners and customers,
						and helping other developers find their way through a system.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section aria-labelledby="path-title">
					<p class="section-label">02 · A T-shaped career</p>
					<h2 id="path-title">Making my way through different domains on all layers</h2>
					<p>
						My route into application development was not a straight web-development path.
						At <a href="https://www.necst.it">NECSTLab</a> during my Computer Science Engineering studies 
						at <a href="https://www.polimi.it">Politecnico di Milano</a>, I worked on FPGA-based high-performance
						computing and cloud orchestration. That research led to papers on FPGA acceleration and serverless
						computing, which you can find in my <a href="/publications">publications</a>.
					</p>
					<p>
						At <a href="https://e-novia.it">e-Novia</a>, I worked across
						industrial software and product contexts: C++ and C#, desktop applications, web systems, 
						and projects in areas including IoT, automotive, robotics, and VR/AR. The variety was challenging,
						but it made me comfortable with different technologies and domains. I also learned how
						software is used in the real, physical world, not only in a browser.
					</p>
					<p>
						Today at Zupit I work closer to the application layer, building and modernising business 
						software with modern .NET, Angular, Azure services, SQL Server, and PostgreSQL. 
						I still benefit from my earlier experiences, but now I'm focused on building software 
						that is maintainable, reliable, and easy to change, all while keeping the user in mind.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section aria-labelledby="exploring-title">
					<p class="section-label">03 · What I’m exploring</p>
					<h2 id="exploring-title">Learning is part of the job.</h2>
					<p>
						I’m continuing to grow as a senior engineer, with a longer-term interest in software architecture
						and systems engineering. I’m reading and experimenting around architectural trade-offs, observability, 
						reliability, distributed-systems concepts, and the engineering practices that make complex software
						less difficult to change.
					</p>
					<p>
						I'm currently exploring Rust as a bridge between product and systems engineering,
						connecting domain thinking and high-level abstractions with performance and low-level engineering.

						I like using a small experiment to understand a system from a different angle: for example, I built a simple
						<a href="/blog/load-balancer-rust-1">load-balancer</a> to understand Rust async and HTTP handling.
						I also regularly exercise with coding challenges.
						My <a href="/projects">projects</a> and <a href="/blog">blog</a> are where I keep those investigations
						visible.
					</p>
				</section>

				<footer class="about-closing">
					<p>
						If you want the concise version, start with my <a href={resumeHref} data-umami-event="click-resume">résumé</a>. 
						If you want to see how I think through technical problems, browse the <a href="/blog">writing</a>.
						And if you’d like to get in touch, you can <a href="/contact" data-umami-event="click-contact-cta" data-umami-event-source-page="about">find me here</a>.
					</p>
				</footer>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about-page {
		max-width: 1080px;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.about-intro {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(280px, 0.85fr);
		gap: clamp(var(--space-xl), 8vw, var(--space-2xl));
		padding: var(--space-xl) 0 clamp(var(--space-xl), 8vw, var(--space-2xl));
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-label,
	.aside-label {
		color: var(--color-accent);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
	}

	.eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--space-md); }

	.about-intro h1 {
		max-width: 720px;
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.75rem);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
		line-height: 1.08;
	}

	.intro-copy {
		align-self: end;
		max-width: 520px;
		font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
	}

	.intro-copy p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
	.lead { font-size: clamp(var(--font-size-lg), 2.5vw, var(--font-size-2xl)); line-height: 1.5; }

	.about-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 0.32fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: clamp(var(--space-xl), 8vw, var(--space-2xl));
		padding-top: var(--space-xl);
	}

	.about-aside { align-self: start; position: sticky; top: 6rem; }
	.aside-label { margin-bottom: var(--space-md); }
	.about-aside dl { margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); }
	.about-aside dl > div { padding: var(--space-sm) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
	.about-aside dl > div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
	dt { color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: var(--font-size-sm); }
	dd { margin: var(--space-xs) 0 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--font-size-sm); line-height: 1.5; }
	.aside-link { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--font-size-sm); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }

	.about-content { max-width: var(--max-width-content); }
	.about-content section { padding-bottom: var(--space-xl); }
	.section-label { margin-bottom: var(--space-md); }
	.about-content h2 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg); font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(var(--font-size-2xl), 4vw, var(--font-size-4xl)); letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
	.about-content p { font-size: 1.05rem; }
	.personal-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: var(--space-xl); }
	.about-closing { border-top: 2px solid var(--color-text); padding: var(--space-lg) 0 var(--space-xl); }
	.about-closing p { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: var(--font-size-lg); }

	@media (max-width: 760px) {
		.about-intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-lg); padding-top: var(--space-md); }
		.intro-copy { align-self: start; }
		.about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-lg); }
		.about-aside { position: static; }
		.about-aside dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--space-sm); }
		.about-aside dl > div, .about-aside dl > div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
	}

	@media (max-width: 520px) {
		.about-aside dl { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.about-aside dl > div { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
	}
</style>
